"""Mutations of part 7a's actors (src/game/clock.*, null_actor.*, wire_cut.*, switch_actor.*,
photo_place.* and frame_box_volume.h) for ../mutfast.py with the actors build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_simple.py --models DIR --build build_item.bat --check check_item.py

Each should make check_item.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Left out as equivalent: the
switch's SetFrame result (the base fails only without a frame, refused before it), SetState's null
parent test (a frame found under the actor's frame has a parent), Toggle's wrap value (0 clamps to
1) and pre-increment (SetState stores the state), StopMission's state store before SetState (SetState
stores it), the photo place's self test in GetMaterialId (the frame's own id again), OnCut's OpenWay
(a client is never a local game), the switch's empty Hit (as the base's), the creators' Destroy
(memory only).

Results (2026-10-26): the first run of 310 caught 304; "wire cut no script" did not compile (fixed)
and 5 survivors needed new cases (a hand under a dummy, the save writer's chunk depth, SetFrame on a
frame with fewer states, the nested switch's log written before the call, a box frame with its own
scale). The rerun: all 310 caught."""
